DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI SlowQueriesPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure
@Observable state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing loading/empty/error/success
plus the 503 subsystem-unavailable variant over an injectable SlowQueriesDataSource seam whose value
types mirror the KMP OperatorConfidence SlowQueriesResponse/SlowQueryRow 1:1 (production binds
OperatorConfidenceStore.slowQueries(orderBy:limit:) through the seam). The page reproduces the web
chrome (title/subtitle), the subsystem-unavailable AlertBanner, and the single top-queries GlassPanel
with an always-visible Order-by + Limit picker pair (re-querying the model on change, web TanStack
queryKey behavior) above an adaptive table — a 7-column columnar Grid on macOS/iPad and per-query
cards on iPhone — covering query fingerprint (monospace, truncated, full text to VoiceOver), call
count, mean/max/total ms, rows, and the shared-buffer cache hit ratio, using the P2 tokens + P3
shared components (no hand-rolled glass; uses TSSelect/TSGlassPanel/TSAlertBanner/TSEmptyState/
TSErrorDisplay/TSSkeleton). Every visible string resolves from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key
names (21 keys added); display formatting (fmtNumber + cacheHitRatio) is ported and unit-tested.
Reachable via a new `.slowQueries` System-sidebar route + `/admin/slow-queries` deep-link alias, wired
into the route-host chain, without displacing the sibling Disk Forecast `.admin` host. Verified on
BOTH idioms by isolated Swift 6 strict-concurrency type-checks (0/0) and an executed model harness
(30/30). The full xcodebuild scheme is RED ONLY due to one pre-existing, out-of-scope shared-surfaces
error (forbidden to commit-fix), with ZERO diagnostics in any of my files.

